                <pb facs="0476" n="469" xml:id="pg469"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/9669: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Phillips</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-08-25T10:00:00+01:00">August 25, 1937—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 25—6:47 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>386. It is announced today that the first battalion of the 10th Regiment of Savoy
                    Grenadiers left Addis Ababa on August 23 for Massawa, where it will embark for
                    Shanghai to reenforce the San Marco Marine battalion in the defense of Italian
                    interests. It is understood that this battalion is composed of between 600 and
                    700 men, including supply troops.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
